KG42.register("rules-d298d83b7dbaae718ec4280a",{"id":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage::v141-c-R001","paper":"32-wholesale_prosumer_storage","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R001","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market clearing","process_stage":"clearing","market_meaning":"P2P allocations are confined to the community. Aggregate purchases must equal aggregate sales multiplied by the P2P conversion and transmission efficiency factor. Scope: Within-community P2P allocations in both stages, for every time step and scenario. Condition: P2P trading is enabled.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function clearing.local under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["clearing.local"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"clearing","context_text":"Within-community P2P allocations in both stages, for every time step and scenario.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e24"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-X","symbol":"X^{(t,h,s)}","meaning":"Overall quantity sold via P2P in both stages by house h in time step t and scenario s, defined in the source as the aggregate of peer-directed P2P sale flows (Eq. 6).","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued electricity quantity; nonnegativity/sign convention not explicitly stated in the supplied evidence","unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e21"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R001-I","symbol":"I^{(t,h,s)}","meaning":"Overall quantity purchased via P2P in both stages by house h in time step t and scenario s, defined in the source as the aggregate of peer-directed P2P purchase flows (Eq. 8).","kind":"operational","domain":"real-valued electricity quantity; nonnegativity/sign convention not explicitly stated in the supplied evidence","unit":null,"indices":["t","h","s"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e23"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R001-psi","symbol":"\\psi^{P2P}","meaning":"Efficiency factor for conversion and transmission of DG sources to P2P sale (Table 1). The source also states that direct P2P trade accounts for a transmission and conversion loss of 7.6%, but the supplied evidence does not explicitly state the numerical efficiency coefficient used in Eq. (9).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":"dimensionless","indices":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e22"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"P2P allocations are confined to the community. Aggregate purchases must equal aggregate sales multiplied by the P2P conversion and transmission efficiency factor. Scope: Within-community P2P allocations in both stages, for every time step and scenario. Condition: P2P trading is enabled.","expression":"\\sum_{h} \\psi^{P2P} \\cdot X^{(t,h,s)} = \\sum_{h} I^{(t,h,s)} \\quad \\forall t \\in T, s \\in S","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["clearing.local"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R001-X","v141-c-R001-I"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R001-psi"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e19","v141-b-g02-e21","v141-b-g02-e24"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p06-c2r4__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"with their fellow peers. To model these P2P interactions, we ap- ces ply a basic transportation mode","equation_id":"Eqs. (6)-(7)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The community allows prosumers the direct trade of electricity with their fellow peers. To model these P2P interactions, we apply a basic transportation model for the trade of electricity. The following equations hold true for both stages. To this end, the overall quantity sold X^{(t,h,s)} in both stages for each house h ∈ H is defined as the sum of all electricity flows X_{p}^{(t,h→p,s)} from this house h ∈ H to its peers p ∈ H, as specified in Eq. (6). X^{(t,h,s)} = \\sum_{p≠h} X_{p}^{(t,h→p,s)} \\qquad (6)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p06-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":6,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"J.M. Zepter, A. Lüth and P. Crespo del Granado et Table 1 Designated sets, parameters and variables ","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":"Table 1","image_ref":"pages/page-06.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Table 1 Designated sets, parameters and variables of the mathematical model. Sets: t ∈ T hours t in time horizon T; h, p ∈ H houses h and peers p in community H; s ∈ S scenarios s in set of scenarios S. Scalars: \\psi^{P2P} efficiency factor for conversion and transmission of DG sources to P2P sale; \\underline{s}/\\overline{s} upper/lower bounds of storage level in battery; α/β maximum charging/discharging rate of battery; η^{c}/η^{d} battery charging/discharging efficiency. Parameters: dem^{(t,h)} demand of house h in time step t; res^{(t,h)} renewable energy production of house h in time step t; \\widetilde{res}^{(t,h,s)} renewable energy production of house h in time step t and scenario s; δ^{(t,h,s)} deviations in production of house h in time step t and scenario s; π_{s} probability of occurrence of renewable scenario s; p_{DA}^{(t)} price of electricity from the grid in the day-ahead market in time step t; p_{ID}^{(t,s)} price of electricity from the grid in the intraday market in time step t and scenario s; p_{F}^{(t)} price of electricity fed into the grid in time step t; p_{P2P}^{(t)} price of electricity in the local market in time step t. Variables: C_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead charge of battery of house h in time step t; C_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday charge of battery of house h in time step t and scenario s; D_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead discharge of battery of house h in time step t; D_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday discharge of battery of house h in time step t and scenario s; F_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead feed of house h in time step t; G_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead grid consumption of house h in time step t; G_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday grid consumption of house h in time step t and scenario s; I_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead P2P electricity purchase of house h in time step t; I_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday P2P electricity purchase of house h in time step t and scenario s; I_{p,ID}^{(t,h←p,s)} intraday P2P electricity purchase of house h from peer p in time step t and scenario s; P^{(t,h)} day-ahead planned electricity supply of house h in time step t; Q^{(t,h)} day-ahead demanded electricity quantity of house h in time step t; S^{(t,h,s)} energy storage level in battery of house h in time step t and scenario s; X_{DA}^{(t,h)} day-ahead P2P electricity sale of house h in time step t; X_{ID}^{(t,h,s)} intraday P2P electricity sale of house h in time step t and scenario s; X_{p,ID}^{(t,h→p,s)} intraday P2P electricity sale of house h from peer p in time step t and scenario s."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"168 J.M. Zepter, A. Lüth and P. Crespo del Granado et al. / account a transmission and conversion lo","equation_id":"Eqs. (8)-(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The sold and purchased quantity can, thus, only stay within the community. The sum of sales over all houses needs to equal the purchases as follows: \\sum_{h} \\psi^{P2P} · X^{(t,h,s)} = \\sum_{h} I^{(t,h,s)} \\quad ∀ t ∈ T, s ∈ S. \\qquad (9)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e22","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"168 J.M. Zepter, A. Lüth and P. Crespo del Granado et al. / account a transmission and conversion lo","equation_id":"Eqs. (8)-(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The direct trade takes into account a transmission and conversion loss \\psi^{P2P} of 7.6% (see [24])."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e23","location":{"location_id":"src-3c39fd6f72-p07-c1r1__v141-a-M01-clearing","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"168 J.M. Zepter, A. Lüth and P. Crespo del Granado et al. / account a transmission and conversion lo","equation_id":"Eqs. (8)-(9)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"The overall purchased quantity per house I^{(t,h,s)} is then specified by Eq. (8). I^{(t,h,s)} = \\sum_{p≠h} I_{p}^{(t,h←p,s)} \\qquad (8)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"clearing.local","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e19","quote":"To model these P2P interactions, we apply a basic transportation model for the trade of electricity. The following equations hold true for both stages."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","quote":"The sold and purchased quantity can, thus, only stay within the community. The sum of sales over all houses needs to equal the purchases as follows: \\sum_{h} \\psi^{P2P} · X^{(t,h,s)} = \\sum_{h} I^{(t,h,s)} \\quad ∀ t ∈ T, s ∈ S. \\qquad (9)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e21","quote":"\\psi^{P2P} efficiency factor for conversion and transmission of DG sources to P2P sale"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"4f0e91b2c356238c54cbd9e8a7faeb7e86684e5453c2dbb525db7b582b732634","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The frozen rule contains an explicit aggregate P2P balance equation in the supplied source evidence (Eq. 9): after applying the P2P conversion/transmission efficiency factor to aggregate sales, total sales equal total purchases for every time step and scenario. The existing C.1 constraint is retained with the same constraint_id, statement, role, members, and original evidence_ids; an explicit source expression and bindings are added. The graph has only clearing.local and no edges, so all bindings attach to that node without inventing graph relationships. B evidence remains unreviewed in this experiment; no independent source audit is claimed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-X","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"X is an aggregate P2P sale quantity used in the local clearing balance. The frozen graph has no variable-specific node, so the variable is attached to the clearing.local relation that owns this balance constraint; no edge is required or invented."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-I","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"I is an aggregate P2P purchase quantity used in the local clearing balance. It is attached to the clearing.local relation that owns the aggregate P2P balance; no frozen edge exists to bind."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-psi","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The efficiency factor scales aggregate P2P sales in the local clearing balance. It is a scalar parameter of the clearing.local relation and has no separate graph node or edge in the frozen graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R001-C001","node_ids":["clearing.local"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"Eq. (9) is the community-level P2P balance constraint governed by clearing.local. The frozen graph contains no edges for this rule, so the constraint is bound to its owning node only, preserving the frozen graph without adding an invented relationship."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
